{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21fd7e39d99b57bc5bcc", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Permutation and Combination - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 60, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924235b"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242353", "title": "Mathematics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422d9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["6176f3e46581241c70729c59"], "question": {"text": "The number of 6-letter words, with or without meaning, that can be formed using the letters of the word MATHS such that any letter that appears in the word must appear at least twice, is _______."}, "options": [{"id": "85f68b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422da"}, {"id": "f71762", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422db"}, {"id": "94e01a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422dc"}, {"id": "d01b90", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422dd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422de", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb7b66f9ce3f243b5123"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8f02"], "question": {"text": "Some couples participated in a mixed doubles badminton tournament. If the number of matches played, so that no couple played in a match, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>840</mn></math>, then the total numbers of persons, who participated in the tournament, is ________."}, "options": [{"id": "e3ada1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422df"}, {"id": "01e5f7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e0"}, {"id": "c78d0c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e1"}, {"id": "168b65", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb7a66f9ce3f243b50f6"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;be the set of all passwords which are six to eight characters long, where each character is either an alphabet from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> or a number from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> with the repetition of characters allowed. If the number of passwords in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> whose at least one character is a number from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "e3e051", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e4"}, {"id": "b38a58", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e5"}, {"id": "34466e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e6"}, {"id": "fc41f0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b44e9"], "question": {"text": "There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> players in a cricket team, out of which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> are bowlers, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> are batsmen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> are wicketkeepers. The number of ways, a team of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;players be selected from them so as to include at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> bowlers, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> batsmen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> wicketkeeper, is"}, "options": [{"id": "692620", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422e9"}, {"id": "ea7981", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422ea"}, {"id": "b8dc8e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422eb"}, {"id": "de36b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422ec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422ed", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d70"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d51"], "question": {"text": "The largest natural number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></math> divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>66</mn><mo>!</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "567530", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422ee"}, {"id": "756dec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422ef"}, {"id": "99cbe2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f0"}, {"id": "87b8c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "For $\\mathrm{n} \\geq 2$, let $S_n$ denote the set of all subsets of $\\{1,2 \\ldots . . ., n\\}$ with no two consecutive numbers. For example $\\{1,3,5\\} \\in \\mathrm{S}_6$, but $\\{1,2,4\\} \\notin \\mathrm{S}_6$. Then $n\\left(\\mathrm{~S}_5\\right)$ is equal to ________"}, "options": [{"id": "45e636", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f3"}, {"id": "572bb4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f4"}, {"id": "4130bc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f5"}, {"id": "d9419c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["6162fc296ed13040ec857615"], "concepts": ["6162fc296ed13040ec8575eb"], "question": {"text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>1</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mn>15</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>15</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>r</mi><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mi>q</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>-</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mmultiscripts></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "6385a5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f8"}, {"id": "153d96", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422f9"}, {"id": "1d4c64", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422fa"}, {"id": "bb8519", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422fb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422fc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["6162fc296ed13040ec857625"], "concepts": ["6162fc296ed13040ec8575fb"], "question": {"text": "In an examination, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> students have been allotted their seats as per their roll numbers. The number of ways, in which none of the students sits on the allotted seat, is"}, "options": [{"id": "11dab5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422fd"}, {"id": "b7b352", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422fe"}, {"id": "b688e6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d92422ff"}, {"id": "a730e8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242300"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242301", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["60e5671b499d1e49588f87fb"], "question": {"text": "The number of 3-digit numbers, formed using the digits $2,3,4,5$ and 7 , when the repetition of digits is not allowed, and which are not divisible by 3 , is equal to__________"}, "options": [{"id": "60545e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242302"}, {"id": "00f227", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242303"}, {"id": "cd5453", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242304"}, {"id": "52c895", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242305"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242306", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb7a66f9ce3f243b50fc"], "question": {"text": "The number of words (with or without meaning) that can be formed from all the letters of the word<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#34;</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></math> in which vowels never come together is....."}, "options": [{"id": "7e6e51", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242307"}, {"id": "6bcaea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242308"}, {"id": "aeb78f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242309"}, {"id": "77d99c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924230a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924230b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54ae"], "question": {"text": "The total number of four digit numbers such that each of the first three digits is divisible by the last digit, is equal to ______."}, "options": [{"id": "9bcf23", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924230c"}, {"id": "bff5bb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924230d"}, {"id": "e86b18", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924230e"}, {"id": "799144", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924230f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242310", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["6162fc286ed13040ec857506"], "question": {"text": "Suppose Anil&#39;s mother wants to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;whole fruits to Anil from a basket of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> red apples, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> white apples and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> oranges. If in the selected <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> fruits, at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> orange, at least one red apple and at least one white apple must be given, then the number of ways, Anil&#39;s mother can offer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> fruits to Anil is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "05ac25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242311"}, {"id": "785406", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242312"}, {"id": "0fe27e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242313"}, {"id": "59c7c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242314"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242315", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["6162fc296ed13040ec857615"], "concepts": ["6162fc296ed13040ec8575eb"], "question": {"text": "The sum of all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-digit numbers less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>,</mo></math> that are formed without using the digit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and they all are multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "4b4f71", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242316"}, {"id": "065590", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242317"}, {"id": "41db84", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242318"}, {"id": "dc5a5f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242319"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924231a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fafa66f9ce3f243b4946"], "question": {"text": "All the letters of the word <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> are written in all possible ways with or without meaning and these words are written as in a dictionary. The serial number of the word <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> IS"}, "options": [{"id": "ad8c64", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924231b"}, {"id": "4f9407", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924231c"}, {"id": "a54152", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924231d"}, {"id": "26bd14", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924231e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924231f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["60e2fbbf66f9ce3f243b549d"], "question": {"text": "The total number of three-digit numbers, with one digit repeated exactly two times, is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "481156", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242320"}, {"id": "7d6379", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242321"}, {"id": "67bfee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242322"}, {"id": "4c7a54", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242323"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242324", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbbf66f9ce3f243b54a1"], "question": {"text": "The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-digit numbers, whose greatest common divisor with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "e4ac6c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242325"}, {"id": "f303b9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242326"}, {"id": "a8906b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242327"}, {"id": "97e6dc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242328"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242329", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "The number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-digit odd numbers, whose sum of digits is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>, is _____."}, "options": [{"id": "819dca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924232a"}, {"id": "6cc5ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924232b"}, {"id": "43f66f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924232c"}, {"id": "551ffb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924232d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924232e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["6162fc296ed13040ec857615"], "concepts": ["6162fc296ed13040ec8575eb"], "question": {"text": "The sum of all the four-digit numbers that can be formed using all the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> is equal to ____."}, "options": [{"id": "bc9195", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d924232f"}, {"id": "d5a395", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242330"}, {"id": "a7f00f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242331"}, {"id": "291b8c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242332"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242333", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4504"], "question": {"text": "The number of ways, 5 boys and 4 girls can sit in a row so that either all the boys sit together or no two boys sit together, is $\\qquad$ -"}, "options": [{"id": "597a7b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242334"}, {"id": "423700", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242335"}, {"id": "62455a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242336"}, {"id": "ae1407", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f242ee0e063d9242337"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69